<h1>Context Menus</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>There are four types of context menus in KUBE :</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="Tree_Context_Menus.htm">Tree Context Menu</a> - It appears when user right clicks on a tree item in <a href="Entities_Pane.htm">Entities Pane</a>. The user can call some basic, visualisation and selection commands from this menu.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="viewport_context_menu.htm">Viewport Context Menu</a> - It appears when user right clicks with the mouse somewhere on the <a href="Viewport.htm">viewable area</a> or on the scroll bars. Some commands are accessible also via the <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="text-decoration:none;"><a href="Toolbar2.htm">toolbar</a></span></u>, <a href="view_menu.htm" target="_self">View Menu</a>, or by <a href="Shortcut_Keys.htm">shortcut keys</a>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><a href="Measure_Context_Menus.htm">Measure Context Menus</a> - these menus appear when working in a specific mode, like Labeling, Dimensioning, etc.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><a href="../Inspection_Mode/User_Interface/Inspection_Context_Menus.htm">Inspection Context Menus</a> - available in Inspection Mode only</p>
</li>
</ul>
